[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/capie/banner.jpg[/img]
[h1]CAPIE[/h1]
[b]Made with AI.[/b] I built this mod with the help of AI tools (Claude Code and Codex), and I say so openly. If you would rather not play mods made with AI, do not download it.

CAPIE (Cyprian's API Extender) is a small native library for Hearts of Iron IV. It lets mods read what the player types into the game's own text field, and it draws custom country names, faction names and flags that are stored in the save. HOI4 script cannot do either on its own. Rename Anything is the first mod built on CAPIE.

This item is the switch. It has no game content and changes no game file: it is only the switch.
[list]
[*]In your playset and enabled: the CAPIE launcher loads CAPIE into the game.
[*]Disabled, or not in the playset: the game starts without CAPIE.
[/list]
Load order does not matter. Keep only one mod called CAPIE: with a local copy of the same name, the game skips this Workshop item. The installer's own local copy is called CAPIE (local copy) and is not installed when you subscribe here.

[b]Pre-release.[/b] Current version: CAPIE 1.6.1 (script API level 8), tested in single player on HOI4 1.19.4.2.

[h2]What's new in 1.6.1[/h2]
[list]
[*]Supports HOI4 1.19.4.2 (the update of 5 November). CAPIE 1.6.0 stays off on it: run the install line below again and choose [i]Install or update[/i].
[*]Updating no longer fails when Windows Defender flags version.dll (a false positive). That optional Proxy loader is now a separate download, so the default install never touches it.
[/list]

[h2]1.6.0[/h2]
[list]
[*]New: country map colours (script API level 8). Mods can give a country any map colour; Rename Anything 0.3.0 uses it. The colour is display only, saved with the game, and goes back to normal without CAPIE.
[*]Faster and safer: CAPIE skips windows that are not its own almost for free and ignores windows the game has destroyed.
[/list]

[h2]Works with total conversions[/h2]
Since switch 1.1.2 there is no CAPIE mark in the main menu any more. The mark needed a copy of the game's main menu file, and that copy replaced the main menu of total conversions such as Kaiserreich, KaiserreduX, The New Order, Millennium Dawn and Old World Blues: their logo, banners and version label were lost. The switch now ships no interface file at all, so every mod keeps its own main menu.
To check that CAPIE runs, open a Rename Anything editor in a game: it shows "CAPIE 1.6 loaded". CAPIE loads about 20 seconds after the main menu appears.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/capie/h-requirements.png[/img]
[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Hearts of Iron IV 1.19.4.2 on Windows.
[*]The CAPIE launcher, set up by the installer. Without it this item does nothing.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/capie/h-installing.png[/img]
[h2]Installing[/h2]
CAPIE installs with a small setup tool. Close Steam, or let the tool close it for you, and pick one of two ways:
[list]
[*][b]One PowerShell line.[/b] Open PowerShell and paste:
[code]irm https://github.com/capie-mods/capie/releases/latest/download/install.ps1 | iex[/code]
A menu opens: choose [i]Install or update[/i].
[*][b]Download from GitHub.[/b] Get the ZIP, install.ps1 and the two release-manifest files from [url=https://github.com/capie-mods/capie/releases/latest]the latest release[/url] into one folder, then in PowerShell in that folder run:
[code].\install.ps1 -Install -PackagePath .\CAPIE-1.6.1-win64.zip[/code]
[/list]
Both ways check the signed release manifest and every file's SHA-256, install into your user folder (never the game folder) and add the CAPIE launcher to the HOI4 launch options in Steam. The same tool updates, installs an older version, switches CAPIE off or uninstalls it.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/capie/h-how-it-works.png[/img]
[h2]How it works[/h2]
When you press Play, the Paradox Launcher writes your playset to dlc_load.json in Documents\Paradox Interactive\Hearts of Iron IV. The CAPIE launcher reads that file after the game has started. If this item is on the list, CAPIE loads once the game reaches the main menu. If the file cannot be read, the game runs without CAPIE and a short notice says so. The game never waits for CAPIE.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/capie/h-safety.png[/img]
[h2]Safety and limits[/h2]
[list]
[*]Game files stay unchanged. The launcher adds nothing to the game folder.
[*]CAPIE opens no network connections.
[*]CAPIE checks the SHA-256 of hoi4.exe and every place it hooks. On any other game build it does not start, and the game runs without it.
[*]Multiplayer has not been tested with two players. Disable this item before you play multiplayer.
[*]Nobody has checked yet whether the game counts this item for the checksum or for achievements.
[*]Some antivirus programs may warn about CAPIE, because it loads itself into the game process. Every release will be scanned on VirusTotal, with the results linked from the release notes.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/capie/h-clean-game.png[/img]
[h2]Back to the clean game[/h2]
Disable this item in the playset and the next start is without CAPIE. To remove CAPIE completely, run the installer and choose Uninstall. Your saves and other mods are not touched.

